  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-anjunganensis-1",
      "html": "<p>Conservation status: Endangered. Parosphromenus anjunganensis stands out from other Parosphromenus species with its prominent red fins outlined with a white band. It is a small freshwater fish belonging to the family Osphronemidae.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-anjunganensis-1",
      "html": "<p>Best kept in small groups of 3-6 in a 5 to 10 gallon (about 19-38 litre) tank with small blackwater fish such as Boraras or mouthbrooding bettas like Albimarginata and Channoides.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-anjunganensis-1",
      "html": "<ul><li>Temperature: 22 – 28 °C</li><li>pH: 3.0 – 6.5</li><li>Hardness: 18 – 72 ppm (about 1 – 4 dGH)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-anjunganensis-1",
      "html": "<p>They are omnivores, feeding on a variety of small invertebrates and insect larvae.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-anjunganensis-1",
      "html": "<p>These fish are generally peaceful and shy, preferring to hide among vegetation or other structures in their environment.</p>"
    }
